--!nonstrict
--[[
	AnimForge — text prompt → playable animation in <Rig>.AnimSaves.

	Tabbed dock: Chat (credit pill, character slot, prompt, result), History
	(every animation and its edits), Settings (account, credits, install link).

	There is no server field, no personal API key and no admin panel here. Every
	generation goes through the Anim Forge server, which is where entitlement,
	the credit spend and metering live; anything settable here would be a way
	around all three. Operator tooling is a separate local-only program.

	Model/provider names never appear in the UI ("Standard" / "Best") — the wire
	values are ambiguous too; real ids live server-side only.

	Rig choice works like Studio's native object pickers (PrimaryPart-style):
	one slot — click it to arm, the cursor becomes a crosshair, hover highlights
	valid rigs and previews their name, click one in the viewport or Explorer and
	it locks in showing only the model's name. Rig type stays internal.
]]

