--[[
	When the server says this build is too old to talk to it, the plugin stops
	being a generator and becomes a single instruction. Everything else is hidden:
	a half-working plugin against a contract it no longer speaks produces
	confusing failures, and the user's only useful action is to update.

	The server enforces the same rule (426 UPDATE_REQUIRED on /v1/generate) — this
	screen is the honest explanation of a refusal that happens regardless.

	Scoped in do...end so its widgets cost the main chunk no registers; only
	`applyUpdateLock` (forward-declared at the top), the `updateLocked` flag the
	entitlement refresh reads, and the address setter escape.
]]
local updateLocked = false
local setUpdateUrl
local setUpdateNudge

--[[
	The gentle half of the same idea: a newer build exists, this one still works.

	Studio updates plugins it installed from the Creator Store; it cannot update
	one dropped into the Plugins folder by hand, and this is. So the only way a
	user ever learns a new build is out is if the plugin says so — and the only
	alternative to saying it here is saying nothing until the hard lockout
	arrives mid-task. Dismissible, and shown once per session: a banner that
	cannot be closed is an advert.
]]
